 "cells": [
  {
   "id": "c1",
   "kind": "markdown",
   "text": "# Molecules that cross the cell: urea\n\n`urea.cif` lists one urea molecule's asymmetric unit (C, O, N, two H) and the eight symmetry operations of P-421m. After\nthe symmetry expansion the two molecules of the cell lie across the cell faces, as in most molecular crystal files.\n**Import structure\u2026** (*Atom style: full*, *bonds* checked) infers the bonds through the periodic cell and writes image\nflags, so\n`urea.data` holds 2 whole molecules with 7 bonds each.\n\nThis notebook only checks the structure (no urea force field is included): after `replicate 3 3 3` there should be\n54 molecules, 378 bonds, and every bond between 1.0 \u00c5 (N-H) and 1.35 \u00c5 (C-N). A molecule broken by the cell faces\nwould show up as a bond longer than the box."
  },
  {
   "id": "c2",
   "kind": "code",
   "text": "units           real\natom_style      full\nboundary        p p p\nread_data       urea.data\nreplicate       3 3 3\npair_style      zero 8.0\npair_coeff      * *\nbond_style      zero\nbond_coeff      *\ncompute         bonds all bond/local dist\ncompute         longest all reduce max c_bonds inputs local\ncompute         shortest all reduce min c_bonds inputs local\ncompute         molecules all chunk/atom molecule\nthermo_style    custom step atoms bonds c_molecules c_shortest c_longest\nrun             0"
  }
 ],
 "inputFiles": {
  "urea.cif": "# Urea, CO(NH2)2, space group P -4 21 m (No. 113), two molecules per cell, from neutron diffraction at 123 K\n# (Swaminathan, Craven and McMullan, Acta Cryst. B40, 300 (1984)): a = 5.565, c = 4.684 Angstrom (rounded values).\n# The N-H...O hydrogen bonds join each molecule to its neighbours across the cell faces. Written for the\n# LAMMPS Web GUI examples.\ndata_urea\n_chemical_formula_sum            'C H4 N2 O'\n_cell_length_a                   5.565\n_cell_length_b                   5.565\n_cell_length_c                   4.684\n_cell_angle_alpha                90.0\n_cell_angle_beta                 90.0\n_cell_angle_gamma                90.0\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M   'P -4 21 m'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number      113\n\nloop_\n_symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz\n'x, y, z'\n'-x, -y, z'\n'y, -x, -z'\n'-y, x, -z'\n'-x+1/2, y+1/2, -z'\n'x+1/2, -y+1/2, -z'\n'-y+1/2, -x+1/2, z'\n'y+1/2, x+1/2, z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\nC1 C 0.0000 0.5000 0.3260\nO1 O 0.0000 0.5000 0.5953\nN1 N 0.1459 0.6459 0.1766\nH1 H 0.2575 0.7575 0.2827\nH2 H 0.1441 0.6441 -0.0380\n",
  "urea.data": "Converted from urea.cif by the LAMMPS workbench\n\n16 atoms\n14 bonds\n4 atom types\n3 bond types\n\n0.000000 5.565000 xlo xhi\n0.000000 5.565000 ylo yhi\n0.000000 4.684000 zlo zhi\n\nMasses\n\n1 12.011 # C\n2 15.999 # O\n3 14.007 # N\n4 1.008 # H\n\nAtoms # full\n\n1 1 1 0 0.000000 2.782500 1.526984 0 0 0 # C\n2 2 1 0 2.782500 0.000000 3.157016 0 0 0 # C\n3 1 2 0 0.000000 2.782500 2.788385 0 0 0 # O\n4 2 2 0 2.782500 0.000000 1.895615 0 0 0 # O\n5 1 3 0 0.811934 3.594434 0.827194 0 0 0 # N\n6 1 3 0 4.753067 1.970566 0.827194 -1 0 0 # N\n7 2 3 0 3.594434 4.753067 3.856806 0 -1 0 # N\n8 2 3 0 1.970567 0.811934 3.856806 0 0 0 # N\n9 1 4 0 1.432988 4.215488 1.324167 0 0 0 # H\n10 1 4 0 4.132013 1.349513 1.324167 -1 0 0 # H\n11 2 4 0 4.215488 4.132013 3.359833 0 -1 0 # H\n12 2 4 0 1.349513 1.432988 3.359833 0 0 0 # H\n13 1 4 0 0.801917 3.584417 4.506008 0 0 -1 # H\n14 1 4 0 4.763084 1.980584 4.506008 -1 0 -1 # H\n15 2 4 0 3.584417 4.763084 0.177992 0 -1 1 # H\n16 2 4 0 1.980584 0.801917 0.177992 0 0 1 # H\n\nBonds\n\n1 1 1 6\n2 2 1 3\n3 1 1 5\n4 1 2 7\n5 2 2 4\n6 1 2 8\n7 3 5 13\n8 3 5 9\n9 3 6 14\n10 3 6 10\n11 3 7 15\n12 3 7 11\n13 3 8 12\n14 3 8 16\n"
 }
